nvas_11"><p class="se-t sie-category-canvas_11-text st-m-paragraph st-d-paragraph">Cupcakes<br></p></a><div data-sid="category-canvas_12" class="sie-category-canvas_12 se"><svg class="se-line"><line  data-d-strokelinecap="butt" data-d-linestyle="solid" data-d-thickness="6" data-d-rotatedwidth="480" data-d-rotatedheight="0" data-d-widthoffset="0" data-d-heightoffset="0" data-d-isround="false" data-d-rotation="0" data-d-roundedsolid="false" data-d-dotted="false" data-d-length="480" data-d-mirrorline="false" data-d-dashwidth="21" data-d-spacing="15" data-d-dasharrayvalue="none" data-m-strokelinecap="butt" data-m-linestyle="solid" data-m-thickness="6" data-m-rotatedwidth="320" data-m-rotatedheight="0" data-m-widthoffset="0" data-m-heightoffset="0" data-m-isround="false" data-m-rotation="0" data-m-roundedsolid="false" data-m-dotted="false" data-m-length="320" data-m-mirrorline="false" data-m-dashwidth="21" data-m-spacing="15" data-m-dasharrayvalue="none" x1="0" y1="0" x2="100%" y2="100%" /></svg></div></div></div></div><div id="content" data-bid="content" class="sb sib-content sb-nm-dH sb-nd-dH"><div class="ss-s ss-bg"><div class="sc" style="width:1200px"><div data-sid="content_0" class="sie-content_0 se"><div class="se-t sie-content_0-text st-m-paragraph st-d-paragraph se-wpt se-rc se-wpt-pc"><input class="jpibfi" type="hidden">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Everything Bagel Buns&#8230;. this might be the easiest recipe I&#8217;ve posted so far. Not to mention it only uses 3 ingredients, and they&#8217;re all super affordable. With everything that&#8217;s happening in the world right now with the recent pandemic, I&#8217;ve been trying to create cheap, delicious eats made with easily attainable items. </p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1356" height="2048" src="https://i0.wp.com/my-messy-kitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/bun5-1-of-1.jpg?fit=636%2C960&amp;ssl=1" alt="" class="wp-image-1381" data-jpibfi-post-excerpt="" data-jpibfi-post-url="https://mymessykitchenn.com/everything-bagel-buns/" data-jpibfi-post-title="Everything Bagel Buns" data-jpibfi-src="https://i0.wp.com/my-messy-kitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/bun5-1-of-1.jpg?fit=636%2C960&amp;ssl=1" srcset="https://i0.wp.com/mymessykitchenn.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/bun5-1-of-1.jpg?w=1356&amp;ssl=1 1356w, https://i0.wp.com/mymessykitchenn.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/bun5-1-of-1.jpg?resize=199%2C300&amp;ssl=1 199w, https://i0.wp.com/mymessykitchenn.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/bun5-1-of-1.jpg?resize=636%2C960&amp;ssl=1 636w, https://i0.wp.com/mymessykitchenn.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/bun5-1-of-1.jpg?resize=768%2C1160&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/mymessykitchenn.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/bun5-1-of-1.jpg?resize=1017%2C1536&amp;ssl=1 1017w, https://i0.wp.com/mymessykitchenn.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/bun5-1-of-1.jpg?resize=1059%2C1600&amp;ssl=1 1059w, https://i0.wp.com/mymessykitchenn.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/bun5-1-of-1.jpg?resize=600%2C906&amp;ssl=1 600w" sizes="(max-width: 960px) 100vw, 960px" /></figure>



<span id="more-1369"></span>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This recipe uses cream cheese, frozen raw dinner rolls, and everything bagel seasoning. I found my bag of 36 frozen dinner rolls for under $4, and for this recipe, I make 8 at a time. I use a #40 scoop for the cream cheese, or just cut the block into small squares, which is about 2 tablespoons per dough ball. Now, I know everyone likes their cream cheese to bagel ratio a little differently. If you&#8217;re someone who likes the cream cheese thinly spread on, feel free to use 1 tablespoon or 2 teaspoons for the filling. I personally like it thick, so this was the perfect amount for me.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1274" height="2048" src="https://i1.wp.com/my-messy-kitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/bun6-1-of-1.jpg?fit=597%2C960&amp;ssl=1" alt="" class="wp-image-1383" data-jpibfi-post-excerpt="" data-jpibfi-post-url="https://mymessykitchenn.com/everything-bagel-buns/" data-jpibfi-post-title="Everything Bagel Buns" data-jpibfi-src="https://i1.wp.com/my-messy-kitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/bun6-1-of-1.jpg?fit=597%2C960&amp;ssl=1" srcset="https://i0.wp.com/mymessykitchenn.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/bun6-1-of-1.jpg?w=1274&amp;ssl=1 1274w, https://i0.wp.com/mymessykitchenn.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/bun6-1-of-1.jpg?resize=187%2C300&amp;ssl=1 187w, https://i0.wp.com/mymessykitchenn.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/bun6-1-of-1.jpg?resize=597%2C960&amp;ssl=1 597w, https://i0.wp.com/mymessykitchenn.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/bun6-1-of-1.jpg?resize=768%2C1235&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/mymessykitchenn.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/bun6-1-of-1.jpg?resize=956%2C1536&amp;ssl=1 956w, https://i0.wp.com/mymessykitchenn.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/bun6-1-of-1.jpg?resize=995%2C1600&amp;ssl=1 995w, https://i0.wp.com/mymessykitchenn.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/bun6-1-of-1.jpg?resize=600%2C965&amp;ssl=1 600w" sizes="(max-width: 960px) 100vw, 960px" /></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">After the frozen dinner rolls defrost for one hour, press them out into a circle on a sheet pan with nonstick cooking spray and scoop the filling inside. Dip your finger in water and wet the outside edges of the dough. Then fold up and pinch the edges together to completely close the seam. Flip the dough so that the pinched edges are flat down the pan. </p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1788" height="2048" src="https://i0.wp.com/my-messy-kitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/bun3-1-of-1.jpg?fit=720%2C825&amp;ssl=1" alt="" class="wp-image-1384" data-jpibfi-post-excerpt="" data-jpibfi-post-url="https://mymessykitchenn.com/everything-bagel-buns/" data-jpibfi-post-title="Everything Bagel Buns" data-jpibfi-src="https://i0.wp.com/my-messy-kitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/bun3-1-of-1.jpg?fit=720%2C825&amp;ssl=1" srcset="https://i0.wp.com/mymessykitchenn.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/bun3-1-of-1.jpg?w=1788&amp;ssl=1 1788w, https://i0.wp.com/mymessykitchenn.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/bun3-1-of-1.jpg?resize=262%2C300&amp;ssl=1 262w, https://i0.wp.com/mymessykitchenn.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/bun3-1-of-1.jpg?resize=838%2C960&amp;ssl=1 838w, https://i0.wp.com/mymessykitchenn.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/bun3-1-of-1.jpg?resize=768%2C880&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/mymessykitchenn.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/bun3-1-of-1.jpg?resize=1341%2C1536&amp;ssl=1 1341w, https://i0.wp.com/mymessykitchenn.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/bun3-1-of-1.jpg?resize=1397%2C1600&amp;ssl=1 1397w, https://i0.wp.com/mymessykitchenn.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/bun3-1-of-1.jpg?resize=600%2C687&amp;ssl=1 600w" sizes="(max-width: 960px) 100vw, 960px" /></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">If you&#8217;d like to bake them now, cover with plastic wrap sprayed with nonstick spray and let them rise for 30 minutes. After 30 minutes, preheat the oven according to the package instructions, although most are 350 degrees. Right before you bake, add everything bagel seasoning to a small bowl and dunk the tops of the dough balls in. If the seasoning isn&#8217;t sticking, you can brush water on top of the dough with your finger or a basting brush and then press them into the seasoning. Bake according to instructions, but mine typically bake in 12-15 minutes. If you&#8217;d like to make them the next day, return to the fridge covered in the saran wrap and remove 1 hour before baking to allow to come to room temperature.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1284" height="2048" src="https://i1.wp.com/my-messy-kitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/bun7-1-of-1.jpg?fit=602%2C960&amp;ssl=1" alt="" class="wp-image-1388" data-jpibfi-post-excerpt="" data-jpibfi-post-url="https://mymessykitchenn.com/everything-bagel-buns/" data-jpibfi-post-title="Everything Bagel Buns" data-jpibfi-src="https://i1.wp.com/my-messy-kitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/bun7-1-of-1.jpg?fit=602%2C960&amp;ssl=1" srcset="https://i0.wp.com/mymessykitchenn.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/bun7-1-of-1.jpg?w=1284&amp;ssl=1 1284w, https://i0.wp.com/mymessykitchenn.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/bun7-1-of-1.jpg?resize=188%2C300&amp;ssl=1 188w, https://i0.wp.com/mymessykitchenn.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/bun7-1-of-1.jpg?resize=602%2C960&amp;ssl=1 602w, https://i0.wp.com/mymessykitchenn.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/bun7-1-of-1.jpg?resize=768%2C1225&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/mymessykitchenn.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/bun7-1-of-1.jpg?resize=963%2C1536&amp;ssl=1 963w, https://i0.wp.com/mymessykitchenn.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/bun7-1-of-1.jpg?resize=1003%2C1600&amp;ssl=1 1003w, https://i0.wp.com/mymessykitchenn.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/bun7-1-of-1.jpg?resize=600%2C957&amp;ssl=1 600w" sizes="(max-width: 960px) 100vw, 960px" /></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This recipe has become a quarantine staple in my house, especially since there are so many other things you can make with the dinner rolls! If you don&#8217;t have everything bagel seasoning, you can make your own or top with whatever bagel topping you like! I&#8217;ve made these with sesame seeds, minced dried onions, or even left them plain! Can&#8217;t wait to hear what you think 🙂 </p>


